{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794770785,"nonce":"3osP1JOr5KuTWmDl7WnMy50F/28=","message":"Step 2 (translucent content under a scroll container on rows) tried and backed out; what it needs.\n\nLifting the `opacity \u003c 1` and `layer_effects` checks from `scroll_node_qualifies` puts a scrolled list with translucent rows on rows (20 of 20 frames), but 19 of 20 frames differ from the vector paint by up to 1,569 px: the rows' backgrounds move and their labels stay where they were painted. A translucent row is a group, and the text in a group that is not under a bound node is drawn by the group text path (glyphs by layer), which gets no slot. Text captured in a bound node's group was put on rows in ec886869 (captured_text.rs, frame_text.rs `refine_captured_text`); the same capture, or slotting the per-layer glyphs to the container's row, is what this step needs.\n\nThe scene \"scroll a translucent list\" stays in animation_paths, held to the vector paint (it is a full paint per frame now), to be added to ON_ROWS when the text moves.","files":null}]}